<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">cast</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">cast</ansi> command attempts to cast a learned spell.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast illum</ansi>
  This would attempt to cast the "Illuminate" spell, if it's in your spell book.

  Spells can also be cast by using their shorthand/ID directly, such as: <ansi fg="command">illum</ansi>

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Combat and Concentration ━━━</ansi>

Casting is an act of held concentration. Spells build over several
rounds as you complete their folds, and taking hits can disrupt the
work — a strong <ansi fg="yellow">Willpower</ansi> keeps your concentration together.

Position matters: casting while grappled or knocked down is much
harder to hold together. If you must cast in a fight, do it on your
feet with room to breathe. Casting counts as a special move and
shares the special-move cooldown.

You cannot begin a cast while crafting or salvaging — finish your
work first.

